1
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:33,480
Alright.

2
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:34,240
Hurry, hurry!

3
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:34,800
Let's go.

4
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:36,360
Li Yiran!

5
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:37,800
Is this how you treat a patient?

6
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:39,280
Don't overdo it.

7
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,720
You really think you're a patient?

8
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:42,280
We'll blow our cover, I'm telling you.

9
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,640
What are you two doing here during class?

10
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:46,800
Which class are you in?

11
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,280
Director Liu.

12
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,440
We're from Class 3, Grade 11.

13
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:50,080
Her stomach hurts.

14
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:51,040
She needs to go to the infirmary.

15
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:56,640
Make it quick.

16
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,360
Okay.

17
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:03,840
Hurry up, we're running out of time!

18
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,000
Hurry!

19
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,920
Hurry it up!

20
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:10,720
The wholesale market is closing soon.

21
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:11,920
Our business will be ruined.

22
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:12,920
Chen Xiaofang.

23
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:15,040
If you put this much energy into studying,

24
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,880
Uncle Chen wouldn't have to come every day.

25
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:19,240
Studying...

26
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:21,240
is all about making big money later.

27
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,640
I'm just taking a shortcut.

28
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:23,840
What do you know?

29
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,840
What are you two doing?

30
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,040
Get down from there, will you?

31
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:34,440
What are you laughing at?

32
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,360
Get down!

33
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:53,520
Give me your hand.

34
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:57,640
Xu Wumei.

35
00:02:58,280 --> 00:02:59,720
That you're a mole for my dad,

36
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:01,560
I've known about it for a while now.

37
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,320
But let me warn you,

38
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,880
if you dare ruin my plans this time...

39
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:08,160
May lightning strike me!

40
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,680
And may I eat without chopsticks for life!

41
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,120
Alright.

42
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:12,000
You said it.

43
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:12,920
I'm leaving.

44
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:13,840
Wait.

45
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:15,920
Ten seconds left.

46
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,600
You've been staring at this phone all day.

47
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,680
What exactly are you trying to do?

48
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:20,560
Young Boss Zhou.

49
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:24,520
The 30-day divorce cooling-off is over.

50
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:28,160
Congrats on regaining your married status!

51
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:29,360
What?

52
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:35,840
Nice job, Wumei!

53
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,120
I didn't say a word to Senior Boss Zhou.

54
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,640
I know.

55
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:41,360
Lady Boss is your life.

56
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:43,120
Beautifully done.

57
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:52,840
Young Boss Zhou,

58
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:56,680
go ahead and boldly win Lady Boss back!

59
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,840
With passion!

60
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:18,480
Cheers!

61
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,600
I was afraid Great-Aunt wouldn't be happy.

62
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,360
My heart was pounding the whole time.

63
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,800
I think she's a pretty nice person.

64
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:30,480
Didn't she also say she'd put

65
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,240
the rest of the money into some...

66
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,560
pet fund, right?

67
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,000
Yeah.

68
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,280
She's such a good person.

69
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:36,080
She is.

70
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:41,800
Have you two paid off your debt yet?

71
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:42,960
Not yet.

72
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,840
We owe Uncle Chen the money now,

73
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:48,640
so we can take our time paying it off.

74
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,400
Dream on.

75
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:04,160
Dad came by today.

76
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,640
The old man is just stubborn.

77
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:06,800
What did he say?

78
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:07,920
He said

79
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:11,760
to let us do what we want.

80
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,280
I really shouldn't have said that.

81
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:25,640
You know,

82
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:27,680
even though Dad doesn't say it,

83
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,280
he understands perfectly.

84
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,040
When I saw him today,

85
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:35,440
I noticed

86
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,600
he has a lot more gray hair now.

87
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,080
It's true.

88
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:46,040
Time flies so fast.

89
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:49,840
Baixi.

90
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:53,640
It really is you.

91
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,480
Everyone's here.

92
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,320
I haven't eaten yet either.

93
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,520
Mind if I join you?

94
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:09,800
What a coincidence, Shiqi.

95
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:22,600
Li Yiran.

96
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:23,960
I really admire you.

97
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,880
You gave up Shanghai just like that.

98
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:28,200
Is your funeral business going well?

99
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:33,720
You see,

100
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,680
am I right?

101
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,520
Your brother is a magnet for rich women.

102
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,320
Chen Baixi brought me to this restaurant.

103
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,440
He said it's really good.

104
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:45,480
Have some more.

105
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,400
I'll go grab a bottle of wine.

106
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,480
Li Yiran,

107
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,560
there's something I want to tell you.

108
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:03,080
I'll go grab some wine too.

109
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:09,960
Go ahead.

110
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,120
Li Yiran,

111
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,840
I like Chen Baixi.

112
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,520
Are you seriously

113
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,560
playing dumb with me?

114
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,520
You like Chen Baixi.

115
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,440
So what?

116
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,440
I'm just telling you,

117
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:27,800
everything is first come, first served.

118
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,680
Everything?

119
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:35,680
Does that apply to love too?

120
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,840
And even if it did,

121
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:40,200
you weren't the first, were you?

122
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:42,080
Fan Shiqi,

123
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,680
don't pull your rich girl act with me.

124
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:47,120
Instead of claiming your territory here,

125
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,120
you should ask Chen Baixi later

126
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:50,720
how he feels about you.

127
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:58,400
You want to

128
00:07:58,400 --> 00:07:59,560
ask me what?

129
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:05,880
He's here in person.

130
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:06,880
Ask him yourself.

131
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,160
I have things to do, I'm leaving.

132
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:31,160
Honey.

133
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,840
Were you waiting for me?

134
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:33,960
Yes, yes.

135
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,920
I was waiting just for you.

136
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,720
Do you remember what day it is today?

137
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,040
What day?

138
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:40,400
Our divorce cooling-off is over.

139
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:41,920
What?

140
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:43,400
The cooling-off is over?

141
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,040
It is.

142
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:50,600
That won't do.

143
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,680
We still need to go to the Civil Bureau.

144
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,560
Let's go, let's go.

145
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:53,280
Why do we still have to go?

146
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:54,080
My bag.

147
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:54,880
Let's go, let's go.

148
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:57,960
Honey.

149
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,200
Chen Baixi.

150
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:03,400
I want to ask you one more time.

151
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,480
I just remembered I have something to do.

152
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:10,600
Boss!

153
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:12,040
Put it on my tab!

154
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,080
Take your time!

155
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:56,920
Hello.

156
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:59,360
The number you dialed is powered off.

157
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,920
Please try again later.

158
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,040
It's eight o'clock.

159
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,360
Still not getting up for work?

160
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,600
Why did you barge in without knocking?

161
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:24,240
I'm going on a blind date today.

162
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,760
I can't be bothered with you.

163
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:30,920
So many clothes, and you don't wash them.

164
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,520
A blind date?

165
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,280
A blind date?

166
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,280
What blind date?

167
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:40,760
Wu Huilian, who's the blind date with?

168
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,800
Why did you bring your dad down here?

169
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,200
My dad and I both want to hear

170
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,000
who you're going on a blind date with.

171
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:00,680
Are you out of your mind?

172
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:02,040
Wu Huilian, I'm telling you,

173
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,640
if you dare do anything to betray my dad,

174
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:04,720
I'll immediately... I'll...

175
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,840
Do you have no filter at all?

176
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:09,440
Knock on wood! Knock on wood!

177
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:10,840
You're really crazy.

178
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:11,840
Old Li, Old Li.

179
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:12,440
Come, come, come.

180
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,960
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

181
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:15,800
There.

182
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,000
Let me put you back up.

183
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,920
Don't you worry about a thing.

184
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:21,880
I would never do anything to betray you.

185
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:23,360
But today,

186
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,960
the situation is a bit special.

187
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:29,040
I really have to get personally involved.

188
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,840
I'm tied up with work, you know.

189
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,200
You can understand that, right?

190
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:45,880
First thing in the morning...

191
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:46,840
What are you yelling for?

192
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,440
Afraid your old man can't hear you?

193
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,160
You're scoffing at me?

194
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:52,480
You didn't wash your hair, did you?

195
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,240
It stinks.

196
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,360
And these clothes of yours.

197
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:55,520
You should wear something more colorful.

198
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:56,280
Even if it's just for work,

199
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,440
you still need to look nice.

200
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,640
Are you out of your mind?

201
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:01,280
Think about what I do for a living.

202
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:01,880
No matter the job,

203
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:02,840
you should still look pretty.

204
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,480
Wearing these drab clothes just won't do.

205
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:05,720
Get out. Get out!

206
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:06,200
I need to pee.

207
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,160
I can't hold it anymore.

208
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:13,280
Stop eavesdropping.

209
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,400
What are you listening to?

210
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,080
I'm listening to my washing machine

211
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,040
to see if it's washing my clothes.

212
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:19,000
I wasn't listening to you.

213
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:20,720
Crazy.

214
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:35,680
Wang Daren still hasn't shown up.

215
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:40,320
You have to face the music eventually.

216
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,040
Wang Daren!

217
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,040
Come in.

218
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:43,840
Come on in!

219
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,200
Stop being so coy.

220
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:45,640
Hurry!

221
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,400
Just look at this.

222
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:52,560
This is the suit Yiran bought me earlier.

223
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,840
It's way too tight on me now.

224
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:55,840
It shrunk.

225
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:57,800
And I don't know how to tie a tie.

226
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,480
Turn around and let me see.

227
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:01,320
Not bad.

228
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:07,680
Not bad.

229
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,000
What are you doing, you crazy woman?

230
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:10,520
You're still in great shape!

231
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:11,400
Wang Daren.

232
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:14,120
Your hair needs a little work.

233
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:15,840
Let's fix it.

234
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:17,320
Leave it to me.

235
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,120
Come here.

236
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:19,320
Come here.

237
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,000
Here.

238
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:39,960
What do you think?

239
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,480
Uncle Daren.

240
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:48,080
The GOAT!

241
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:49,720
Badass!

242
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,080
Take a look.

243
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:53,240
See for yourself.

244
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:56,320
It's really good.

245
00:14:58,640 --> 00:14:59,600
Looks great.

246
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,320
Two crazy women.

247
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:05,600
Wang Daren.

248
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:06,600
Forty-nine.

249
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:07,280
Hardworking.

250
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:07,920
Brave.

251
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:09,640
A lifelong hustler and a classic nice guy.

252
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:11,320
And a small business owner.

253
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,840
Wang Daren.

254
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,040
Be more confident.

255
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:22,800
Coming!

256
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,520
Sorry.

257
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:45,760
I'm late.

258
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,000
You must be Daren.

259
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,080
That's me.

260
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:55,560
I just picked these by the road.

261
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,360
They don't compare to yours.

262
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:05,880
Your hair is quite unique.

263
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,640
I just had it styled.

264
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:11,600
Huh?

265
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:14,160
Why do you smell like barbecue?

266
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:17,520
I run a barbecue stand.

267
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:24,760
Don't worry, Daren.

268
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:26,560
I'm Feng.

269
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,240
A widow for three years.

270
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:29,680
What I'm looking for

271
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:31,200
is an honest man.

272
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,560
So let me ask you,

273
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:42,120
is your pension this much?

274
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:45,960
I don't have a pension.

275
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:46,760
What?

276
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,240
Aren't you a business owner?

277
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:51,040
How can you not have a pension?

278
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:54,920
Then...

279
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:56,480
how much savings do you have?

280
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,080
I do have some.

281
00:16:59,080 --> 00:16:59,960
I have five...

282
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:01,040
What?

283
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:02,600
Fifty thousand.

284
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,040
You call fifty thousand "savings"?

285
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:04,760
I actually...

286
00:17:05,840 --> 00:17:07,960
How can you even go on a blind date?

287
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,760
You look decent enough,

288
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:12,080
but with what you have to offer,

289
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:13,440
you want to find a wife?

290
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,400
You're way out of your league.

291
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,200
Unbelievable.

292
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,840
Wasting my time.

293
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:24,440
My bracelet alone is worth over 50,000.

294
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,640
I even permed my hair for this.

295
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:29,080
I'm so angry. Seriously.

296
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:37,120
Huilian!

297
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:40,000
What kind of guy did you set me up with?

298
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,440
I never want to go on a blind date again!

299
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:45,480
Daren.

300
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:47,040
This one's no good.

301
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:49,240
She's too materialistic.

302
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,160
Let's go.

303
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:50,960
On to the next one.

304
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:51,760
I'm not going.

305
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:53,760
The next one is an educated woman.

306
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:54,360
Beautiful,

307
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:54,840
and absolutely wonderful.

308
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:55,680
Let's go!

309
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:56,400
Feng,

310
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:58,080
I admit I misjudged her.

311
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,400
But this one is great.

312
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:00,640
She's a real catch.

313
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:01,680
She's never even dated before.

314
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:02,240
Let me tell you,

315
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,480
she's highly educated too.

316
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:06,760
Look,

317
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,040
I didn't even finish middle school.

318
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:16,160
I'm uneducated.

319
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,440
I'm clearly not good enough for her.

320
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:18,320
Forget it. Never mind.

321
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:22,000
What's the matter with you?

322
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:27,080
Do you know why people are lonely?

323
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:29,560
They're afraid to take a step forward.

324
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,160
Be a little braver!

325
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:31,960
Life is short.

326
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:33,080
Take that step forward.

327
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,680
What? Do you need me to help you up?

328
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:38,680
I'll go, I'll go.

329
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:56,920
You must be Miss Lin.

330
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:00,320
I'm Wang Daren.

331
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:02,760
"Ren" as in benevolence.

332
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:05,560
You're Mr. Wang.

333
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,640
Just call me Old Wang.

334
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,160
Have a seat.

335
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:11,400
Thank you.

336
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:19,160
Do you have a favorite author?

337
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:22,040
An author?

338
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:22,760
Yes.

339
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:25,920
I like the author of Journey to the West.

340
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:26,680
Wu Sangui.

341
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,720
Have you read this book then?

342
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:33,880
No.

343
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,720
But I have read books.

344
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:38,760
I read a book at the mine.

345
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,680
Called "How Barbecue Was..."

346
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,120
No...

347
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:43,080
Steel.

348
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:44,960
How Steel Was...

349
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,240
Tempered.

350
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,760
How the Steel Was Tempered.

351
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:50,000
It was tempered nicely.

352
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:52,960
You flatter me.

353
00:19:58,240 --> 00:19:59,080
Mr. Wang.

354
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:00,440
Do you believe in fate?

355
00:20:01,040 --> 00:20:02,040
I do.

356
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:02,840
You believe it too?

357
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:04,160
Looking at your face,

358
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:05,920
your marriage palace shows ill omens.

359
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:06,880
At best, you'll lose money.

360
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:08,840
At worst, there will be bloodshed.

361
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:10,680
We're not a good match.

362
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:11,720
I'll take my leave.

363
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:13,960
Wait.

364
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:17,000
Why would I have bloodshed?

365
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:18,560
What are you talking about?

366
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:20,000
Nonsense.

367
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:25,600
She's really quite annoying.

368
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:28,320
And she's supposed to be educated.

369
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:30,320
You only have yourself to blame.

370
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:31,720
I told you,

371
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:32,640
I'm not good enough for her.

372
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:33,680
You just wouldn't listen.

373
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:39,120
Don't be mad.

374
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:42,800
You actually look pretty handsome today.

375
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:46,040
Really?

376
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:49,600
Except your hair is a bit weird.

377
00:20:49,640 --> 00:20:51,360
I think my hair looks the best.

378
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,440
Okay, okay, okay.

379
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,280
You're the boss.

380
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:56,200
I'm sorry about today.

381
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,640
Let me treat you to Western food.

382
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:59,000
What Western food?

383
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,840
KFC. Let's go.

384
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:02,440
What C?

385
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:04,040
What is it?

386
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:04,840
What is it really?

387
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:05,640
KFC. KFC.

388
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:06,640
So damn annoying.

389
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,760
No matter how beautiful,

390
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:13,320
nothing is more beautiful than kindness.

391
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:14,800
No matter how educated,

392
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,320
conscience is still more important.

393
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:19,080
Those two women don't deserve you.

394
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:21,160
It's fine.

395
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:23,080
I'm used to being alone.

396
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,480
But what about you?

397
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:27,520
Haven't thought about finding someone else?

398
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:30,840
Never crossed my mind.

399
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:34,240
Actually, I still can't let go of Old Li.

400
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:36,040
I haven't thought about these things.

401
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,400
All right.

402
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:41,080
You should think about yourself too.

403
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,760
Didn't you say it yourself?

404
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:44,080
Why are people lonely?

405
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:47,720
You're just afraid to take that step now.

406
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,080
I'm not lonely.

407
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:56,320
I have my Li Yiran.

408
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:57,720
Why would I be lonely?

409
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,680
Yiran will get married sooner or later.

410
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:01,560
You've got a long life ahead of you.

411
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:02,680
Yeah.

412
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:04,480
With such a long journey ahead,

413
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:06,040
do you really plan to walk it alone?

414
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:08,680
You should find someone to marry.

415
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:09,440
Later on,

416
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:11,080
when you want to chat,

417
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:13,000
you'll always have someone to talk to.

418
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:16,080
Sleeping next to someone

419
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:17,960
is always better than sleeping alone.

420
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,000
You know?

421
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:20,640
Alright, alright.

422
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:22,000
I get it, I get it.

423
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:26,440
I know you mean well.

424
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:27,800
I'll think it over when I get back.

425
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:30,000
You still need to think it over?

426
00:22:31,040 --> 00:22:32,960
Your hair has gone completely white.

427
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:35,000
Go get it dyed at Zhang Lijuan's someday.

428
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:36,920
Will do, will do.

429
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:37,760
I'm heading out.

430
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:38,240
Off you go.

431
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:40,440
Take care.

432
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:41,400
Got it!

433
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:09,120
Getting married.

434
00:23:09,120 --> 00:23:10,000
Sleeping together.

435
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:12,240
Is that right?

436
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:15,320
Are middle-aged people this wild now?

437
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:17,320
My god.

438
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:25,720
Tangtang and Afu got their wedding photos.

439
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:27,880
How are they doing?

440
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:33,440
Those two kids are getting so skinny.

441
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,280
Especially Afu.

442
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,640
He's so skinny, it's just...

443
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:38,880
It breaks my heart just looking at him.

444
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,600
Young Boss Zhou even cried.

445
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:44,560
We want to do something to help them.

446
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:46,880
But there's nothing we can do.

447
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:51,000
I'll go visit them one of these days.

448
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:52,440
Oh, right.

449
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,840
We have a lot of supplements at home.

450
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:55,040
We don't take them anyway.

451
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:56,600
You should just bring them over.

452
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:57,560
Sure.

453
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,040
Wu Huilian.

454
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:02,880
Let me ask you something.

455
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,000
Go ahead.

456
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:06,000
Tell me...

457
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:09,000
What do you think about love?

458
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:13,680
I want to date you with marriage in mind.

459
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:16,040
I never thought about marrying you.

460
00:24:16,040 --> 00:24:16,800
No.

461
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:20,760
I never thought about dating you.

462
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:22,640
That's not it either. It's just...

463
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:23,760
Age is not an issue.

464
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:26,440
Let's build a beautiful new life together.

465
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:32,640
At my age,

466
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:34,080
why talk about love?

467
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:35,800
It's a million miles away from me.

468
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:41,920
Actually, in this life,

469
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:44,720
nothing truly belongs to you.

470
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,640
If you lose something,

471
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:48,280
it's okay to just be sad for a bit.

472
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:50,280
Most of the time, you're left with regret.

473
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:53,960
Do you have regrets about anyone?

474
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:04,720
I have regrets about you.

475
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,360
You're already twenty-six,

476
00:25:06,360 --> 00:25:07,240
and you're still not married.

477
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:08,560
When I was your age,

478
00:25:08,560 --> 00:25:10,320
you were already writing essays, you know?

479
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:11,920
And you'd solved so many math problems!

480
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:13,440
What's this about getting married?

481
00:25:13,440 --> 00:25:14,200
Just eat your watermelon.

482
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:15,640
Stop asking so many questions.

483
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:17,640
Didn't you ask me what love was first?

484
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:18,920
I asked you, so just answer.

485
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:20,320
You're so weird.

486
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:21,200
It's fine when you ask me,

487
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,320
but it's not okay when I ask you?

488
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:24,200
What kind of watermelon did you buy?

489
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,000
It has so many seeds.

490
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:26,440
And it's not sweet at all.

491
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,160
I'm done eating.

492
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:38,320
Whether the watermelon is sweet or not,

493
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:39,680
only you know in your heart.

494
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,440
Old Li.

495
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:48,800
I did reject him.

496
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:49,800
You're up in heaven,

497
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:51,160
you saw that, right?

498
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:14,800
What are you doing?

499
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:16,160
Sneaking around?

500
00:26:17,240 --> 00:26:18,200
Is Dad here?

501
00:26:18,640 --> 00:26:19,440
He's not here.

502
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:26,280
Look.

503
00:26:26,280 --> 00:26:27,080
The samples.

504
00:26:30,080 --> 00:26:31,720
And also,

505
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:34,280
the flyers I printed.

506
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:35,480
We'll go hand them out later.

507
00:26:37,040 --> 00:26:39,360
Isn't it bad to act first and ask later?

508
00:26:40,240 --> 00:26:41,280
What are you afraid of?

509
00:26:41,720 --> 00:26:42,840
Worst case scenario,

510
00:26:42,840 --> 00:26:46,920
I'll use the money from Zhou Fang's dad

511
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:48,680
to start my own business.

512
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:51,560
Then I'll be the big boss,

513
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:53,360
and you can be my second-in-command.

514
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:56,000
Then,

515
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:57,120
Dad,

516
00:26:58,240 --> 00:26:59,160
what about him?

517
00:27:00,640 --> 00:27:01,680
Dad is getting old.

518
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:03,000
He has to retire sooner or later.

519
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,920
We'll make him

520
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:07,680
a funeral consultant.

521
00:27:08,320 --> 00:27:09,480
Now I get it.

522
00:27:09,480 --> 00:27:11,880
You think our dad is too old.

523
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,640
How could I think he's too old?

524
00:27:14,080 --> 00:27:16,040
I just think he's a bit stubborn.

525
00:27:17,760 --> 00:27:19,440
Then tell me the truth.

526
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:22,040
Have you been planning to take over?

527
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:24,640
It's letting the capable take charge.

528
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:26,640
Chen Xiaofang,

529
00:27:28,080 --> 00:27:29,680
you think you're all grown up now, huh?

530
00:27:30,120 --> 00:27:32,400
You've even planned my funeral for me!

531
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:33,720
Dad!

532
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:35,520
Why didn't you tell us you were back?

533
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:38,080
Tell you I'm back?

534
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:41,000
How else would I hear your rebellion?

535
00:27:41,320 --> 00:27:42,160
Dad,

536
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:44,080
how could I be planning a rebellion?

537
00:27:44,080 --> 00:27:46,280
I'm just expanding our business for you.

538
00:27:46,280 --> 00:27:47,720
Don't give me that.

539
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:51,840
Didn't you see it yourself?

540
00:27:51,840 --> 00:27:52,800
When Duoduo passed away,

541
00:27:52,800 --> 00:27:55,520
Zhou Fang's great-aunt cried so hard.

542
00:27:57,240 --> 00:27:59,160
Do you remember Granny Li next door?

543
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:01,640
She raised Dahuang like her own son.

544
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:03,880
But when Dahuang passed away,

545
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:06,240
he didn't even have a decent urn.

546
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:07,360
He was just hastily buried.

547
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:08,640
It was so pitiful.

548
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:12,600
Chen Baixi.

549
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:14,560
Go.

550
00:28:15,280 --> 00:28:16,080
Go do what?

551
00:28:16,080 --> 00:28:17,960
Go hand out these flyers.

552
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:20,600
For real?

553
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:22,760
Obviously.

554
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:26,080
How can we expand without handing them out?

555
00:28:26,800 --> 00:28:28,160
Dad,

556
00:28:28,160 --> 00:28:30,520
I knew you were the best!

557
00:28:30,520 --> 00:28:32,120
I love you! I love you!

558
00:28:32,360 --> 00:28:34,440
That's enough, that's enough.

559
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:38,280
I haven't finished speaking yet.

560
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,000
What is it?

561
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:42,200
Before I retire,

562
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:44,440
don't even think about taking over.

563
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:46,040
Yes, sir!

564
00:28:54,480 --> 00:28:55,360
Happy now?

565
00:28:57,640 --> 00:28:58,840
You said yes, but you still hit me.

566
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:00,320
Let's go.

567
00:29:00,320 --> 00:29:00,800
I'm hitting you anyway.

568
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:02,440
Let's hand out flyers.

569
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:05,320
We've added new services.

570
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:07,040
New services added.

571
00:29:07,280 --> 00:29:08,120
Give me some.

572
00:29:08,560 --> 00:29:09,360
Let's go.

573
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:15,280
Huilian, are you playing or not?

574
00:29:16,080 --> 00:29:18,200
Are you looking at your phone or playing?

575
00:29:18,880 --> 00:29:20,840
I'm swamped with work, you know.

576
00:29:21,640 --> 00:29:22,720
It's my turn to draw.

577
00:29:23,760 --> 00:29:24,560
Five Dots.

578
00:29:25,720 --> 00:29:26,720
If you ask me,

579
00:29:26,760 --> 00:29:29,040
people dating these days,

580
